libfacts (2.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * C++: FACT(a op b) writes the comparison directly and still prints both
    values; FACT(a op b, note) adds a footnote built only for a fiction.
  * FACT(a,op,b) evaluates each side once in C with gcc or clang and in C++;
    elsewhere the console report warns when a run evaluated twice.
    New symbol: facts_twice.
  * The printed gdb hint runs with --facts_unsafe, so its breakpoints are
    reached under safe execution.
  * FACTS_TRACE and FACTS_WATCH build without warnings under -Wall -Wextra.
  * The console and JUnit reports are separated from the run; output is
    unchanged apart from the gdb hint.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libfacts (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Safe execution: fork/exec wrapper with crash detection, timeout, niceness.
  * Runtime test registration via --facts_find (dlsym-based).
  * --facts_register_all to print FACTS_REGISTER_ALL block.
  * Removed auto-discovery (memory scanning). Explicit registration required.
  * New CLI options: --facts_unsafe, --facts_timeout=N.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
